{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KY", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[II Proposition 7.2.3]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{lemma-valuative-criterion-separatedness}\n", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}[", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf92702a406e0be4bfe42638f265724bf48687b6154e052774fa4c352515d032", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8cae5ed3f34871491f219a1dce99ec6336ec13790c9054516019a6e57be12abf", "source_text": "Valuative criterion separatedness<OWNARGEND_0001><LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism.\nAssume\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the morphism <MATH_0002> is quasi-separated, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the morphism <MATH_0003> satisfies the uniqueness\npart of the valuative criterion.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen <MATH_0004> is separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa9ce14f1f4d985a2f4e006f7e33e7cb6dc0f1673eca3969542c9d6e1ff8fe1c", "unit_id": "tag:01L0:statement"}
